.TH ASTERCTL-BLOB-READ 1 "2026-10-16" "Aster" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
asterctl-blob-read \- read an authenticated Aster Blob to a new local file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY asterctl
.RI [ GLOBAL-OPTIONS ]
.B blob-read
.BI \-\-id " ID"
.BI \-\-topic " TOPIC"
.BI \-\-scope " SCOPE"
.BI \-\-output " PATH"
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B asterctl blob-read
streams a Blob from a running Aster agent into a newly created local file.
It validates contiguous offsets, bounded pages, stable immutable metadata and
TTL, the authenticated completion marker, and the exact declared total length.
.PP
On Linux, the destination directory must be owner-controlled: owned by the
current user and not writable by group or other users. Bytes are written to a
randomly named mode-0600 sibling. After the complete file is synchronized, the
command atomically renames that exact inode with no-replace semantics and
synchronizes the directory. The command never overwrites an existing or
concurrently created destination.
.PP
The command fails before contacting the agent on non-Linux platforms and when
the destination filesystem cannot provide named staging, atomic no-replace
rename, or directory synchronization. Failure cleanup removes the sibling on a
best-effort basis; filesystem errors or abrupt process or host failure can
leave the hidden owner-only file for operator cleanup. If synchronization fails
after publication, the error says that the output exists and must be verified
before retrying.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-id " ID"
Required Blob ID as Base64-encoded 32 bytes.
.TP
.BI \-\-topic " TOPIC"
Required exact Blob topic.
.TP
.BI \-\-scope " SCOPE"
Required exact Blob scope.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " PATH"
Required destination path. It must not already exist.
.SH OUTPUT
Blob bytes are written only to
.BR \-\-output .
After a complete verified stream, stdout reports Blob ID, publisher, publisher
counter, topic, scope, priority, total length, optional media type, schema ID,
acceptance marker, and original TTL. It never prints Blob plaintext.
.PP
Text renders TTL as exactly
.B TTL: durable
or
.BR "TTL: MILLISECONDS ms" .
Finite JSON uses an exact decimal string in
.BR ttlMs ;
durable JSON omits that field.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The complete verified Blob was written.
.TP
.B 1
Read or local-file handling failed. The requested output remains absent before
publication; staging cleanup is best-effort.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid or missing arguments.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR asterctl (1),
.BR asterctl-blob-publish (1)
